      "statement": "PromptDock builds the outgoing message in send(): it renders the step focus (when a step is chosen) and the reverse-mode focus (when the mode is on), filters out the empty strings, joins the remaining prefixes with newlines and appends the trimmed draft, so a message with only a step carries exactly one prefix line and a message with neither goes out unchanged.",
